# Where the data lives.
#
# Local development always uses a plain SQLite file at data/app.db, created and
# migrated on first query. Nothing to set up.
#
# Turso's Vercel integration injects TURSO_DATABASE_URL and TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN,
# and the app reads those names directly. `vercel env pull` writes them into
# .env.local, which Next also loads for `pnpm dev` - so they are honoured only
# in production, or when something opts in on purpose:
#
#   pnpm db:push:remote        apply the schema to the deployment's database
#   pnpm smoke:remote          read/write check against the deployment
#   pnpm copy-up --yes         copy the local database up
#
# To point one command anywhere at all, set an explicit target - this always
# wins, in any environment:
#
#   KITAAB_DB_URL=file:/tmp/scratch.db pnpm check
#   KITAAB_DB_URL=libsql://... KITAAB_DB_TOKEN=... pnpm smoke
